<title>INDIA: India's ITC 1996/97 net higher.</title>
<headline>India's ITC 1996/97 net higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	  3,426.5	vs   2,610.8</p>
<p>    Gross Income     59,523.7	vs  51,878.6</p>
<p>    Net income	 29,989.7	vs  26,082.3</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit    5,822.5	vs   4,522.3</p>
<p>    Other income	  896.1	vs     725.1</p>
<p>    Expenditure	22,336.1	vs  20,243.6</p>
<p>    Interest	    1,200.8	vs     839.0</p>
<p>    Gross Profit	6,452.8	vs   4,999.7</p>
<p>    Depreciation	  630.3	vs     477.4</p>
<p>    Tax		   2,396.0	vs   1,911.5</p>
<p>Note - Tobacco conglomerate ITC Ltd is 31.7 percent owned by Britain's B.A.T Industries Plc.</p>
<p>The latest results are unaudited.</p>
<p>Exports from its tobacco division rose 70 percent to 2.56 billion rupees from 1.50 billion in 1995/96, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The company's board has approved capital expenditure/investment plan of 19 billion rupees over next five years, it said without giving details.</p>
<p>The statement said government investigations were continuing against &quot;past and present&quot; company officials for alleged violations of several laws.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
</text>
